        "title": "Logistics and Supply Chain",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Logistics is the discipline of moving the right thing to the right place at the right time at the right cost. Supply chain management adds the upstream dimension: design the entire network of suppliers, manufacturers, distributors, and customers so that products flow efficiently. The 2020-2022 disruptions demonstrated that supply chains optimized purely for efficiency are fragile — resilience requires redundancy, which costs money."
